      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-304962",
      ":question/problem": "A national park contains $5$ mountain trails and $6$ valley trails. Each mountain trail has $12$ sightings of eagles and $4$ sightings of hawks. Each valley trail has $7$ sightings of eagles and $9$ sightings of hawks. A sighting from one of these trails is selected at random. What is the probability that the sighting occurred on a valley trail, given that the animal spotted was an eagle?"
