      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-304963",
      ":question/problem": "A bird sanctuary contains $8$ forest paths and $3$ riverside paths. Each forest path has $9$ sightings of owls and $6$ sightings of woodpeckers. Each riverside path has $5$ sightings of owls and $7$ sightings of woodpeckers. A sighting from one of these paths is selected at random. What is the probability that the sighting occurred on a riverside path, given that the animal spotted was an owl?"
